# Weight FILES are large and separately licensed; git is the wrong tool for them. The
# RECORDS beside them are the opposite -- PROVENANCE.json is the only thing that says what
# the bytes are, and `/models/*` was swallowing it along with NAMES.md, licenses/ and the
# README. A manifest that is not in the repository cannot be the manifest.
/models/*
!/models/.gitkeep
!/models/README.md
!/models/PROVENANCE.json
!/models/NAMES.md
!/models/licenses/
!/models/licenses/**
!/models/docs/
!/models/docs/**
# The weight directory itself must be re-included before a file inside it can be: git cannot
# re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is excluded, so `!/models/llm/README.md` alone did
# nothing. Re-include the directory, exclude its contents, keep the one document.
!/models/llm/
/models/llm/*
!/models/llm/README.md
*.gguf
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.pt
*.onnx

# Runtime state. Regenerated; never a source of truth -- the LOCK, the logs, the pid, the
# generated page, and api.env which is mode 600 and must never be committed or printed.
#
# `/run/` alone excluded the directory, and git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded -- so run/README.md, the only thing in there that explains any of
# it, could not be tracked no matter what came after. A clone got an absent directory and
# no answer to "what is run/". Exclude the CONTENTS instead, and keep the one document.
/run/*
!/run/README.md
*.log

# Dependency trees, in every language this repo touches.
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.next/
dist/
target/

# `build/` unanchored, which is what stood here, matches ANY directory named build at any
# depth -- and it silently swallowed tools/build/, all 32 generators. build_progress.py,
# build_ports.py, build_pages.py and build_component_readmes.py were untracked for the whole
# life of this tree, so a clone got none of the things that write this repository's records.
# Found by checking a README somebody said was missing; it was there and ignored.
#
# Anchored to the engine trees, which is the only place build output actually lands here.
/symoneural-*/build/
/*/build/
!/tools/build/

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
